 "about_text": "Michael Kohn Gallery was founded in 1985 by Michael Kohn, opening first on Robertson Boulevard in West Hollywood before relocating in 2014 to its current home on North Highland Avenue in Los Angeles. The gallery presents historically grounded exhibitions alongside a contemporary program, linking postwar West Coast movements such as Beat assemblage, Light and Space, and California Minimalism to newer generations of painters and sculptors. It represents senior West Coast figures including Lita Albuquerque and Sharon Ellis, oversees the estates of Bruce Conner, Wallace Berman, Joe Goode, and Martha Alf, and maintains a growing roster of emerging and mid-career artists working internationally, spanning painting, assemblage, and mixed-media practice with an emphasis on figuration, identity, and material experimentation.",
 "source_kind": "official",
